2. Modifications made for libms-studio (required by §4(b))
----------------------------------------------------------

  Project: libms-studio / 里白造物拼豆图纸生成器

  - Extracted the conversion core out of a browser IIFE closure into pure ESM
    functions with explicit parameters. The upstream code relied on closure state
    (`state`, `els`, `PALETTE`) and on `convertPixels.toString()` being serialized
    into a Blob Worker.
  - Removed every DOM, Canvas, Worker, localStorage, i18n and UI-state dependency.
    The Canvas rasterization stage was reimplemented as pure typed-array resampling
    in `raster.mjs`; the host now supplies the initial ImageData.
  - Lifted all hard-coded numeric thresholds into `config.mjs` as named constants,
    each recording the upstream value it came from (`BGS_CONFIG_META`).
  - Replaced the Blob-Worker `toString()` serialization with standard ESM imports.
  - Removed the upstream 5-bit bucketed nearest-colour LUT and its shared
    `+32768` array offset; exact-colour matching and CIEDE2000 selection are
    unchanged, only the cache changed.
  - Removed the legacy 64-colour palette migration map (no libms equivalent).
  - Removed silent clamping of user-supplied grid sizes; out-of-range requests are
    now reported in `diagnostics.geometry.limits` instead of being rewritten.
  - Repaired a tautological guard in the auto-crop decision
    (`retainedInkRatio` was identically 1 upstream) so that it actually measures
    retained ink.
  - Added Otsu plateau handling to match the correction already applied to libms's
    own `legend-text-parse.js`.
  - Added an options-driven public entry point, `convertImageToBeads(imageData,
    options)`, and a new A/B comparison layer (`ab-test.mjs`, `statistics.mjs`)
    that did not exist upstream.
  - Did NOT copy the upstream palette data files (`src/palettes/mard221.js`,
    `src/palettes/catalog.js`). libms uses its own palette catalogue. See §3.

  Modified files are marked with a header comment naming the upstream location and
  summarising the deviation.


